The Supreme Court has exclusive original jurisdiction  (Article 131) to decide legal disputes arising between: 
(a)	 The Centre and a State;
(b)	 The Centre and a State on one side, and another State on the other side;
(c)	 Inter-state disputes, such as river water disputes, etc.
